| `ci_pipeline.gitlab_image` | string | `ci-image.example.invalid/python{python}-node{node_major}` | an image reference, its `{name}` fields filled from `toolchain` | `tests/ci_adapters.py`; `tests/integration/test_ci_pipeline_gate.py` | Names the image the GitLab adapter's job runs in; the gate fails a `.gitlab-ci.yml` whose `image:` line is not this value filled from `toolchain`. Keel has verified no public image that carries both the Python and the Node major, so the default is a host under `.invalid`, which never resolves: point this key and the file's `image:` line at an image that carries both. | the GitHub adapter, whose setup steps install the toolchain: `toolchain.python`, `toolchain.node_major` | always |
